/**
 * # Used NX tags to enforce module boundaries
 *
 * ## Scopes of tags:
 * - `application:*` — Applications. **MUST NOT** be reused across different projects.
 * - `mf:*` — Microfrontends. **MUST ONLY** be reused according to the MF logic.
 * - `router:*` — UI libraries that are used as routers. **MUST ONLY** be reused in frontend apps or microfrontends.
 * - `ui:*` — UI libraries. **MUST NOT** be reused in `pure:*`, `server:*` or `application:backend`.
 * - `server:*` — Server libraries. **MUST NOT** be reused in `pure:*`, `ui:*`, `mf:*` or `application:frontend`.
 * - `pure:*` — Libraries without any framework-specific logic. Can be reused in any project.
 * - `nx:*` — Libraries that are used internally in NX-plugins. **MUST NOT** be reused in any project!
 *
 * ## Some important second dimensions:
 *
 * - `*:frontend` — Browser-based apps. **MUST NOT** mess with the server-side logic.
 * - `*:backend` — Server-side apps. **MUST NOT** mess with the server-side logic.
 * - `*:internal` — Libraries that are not intended to be published. **MUST NOT** be used in `**:publishable` projects.
 * - `*:publishable` — Libraries that are intended to be published. Has no restrictions in terms of reuse (excluding scopes).
 *
 * @see https://nx.dev/docs/guides/enforce-module-boundaries/tag-multiple-dimensions
 */
/* eslint-enable max-len */

